easy.body:
Easy mode is made for learning:

• you start with €3M instead of €2M;
• at most 2 random cards per sprint instead of 3 (the Friday 5pm outage can still add one);
• the negative effects of crises are halved.

Easy mode scores have their own leaderboard: they don't count in the global leaderboard.

normal.body:
This is the classic game, the one the balance is tuned for:

• €2M to start and 18 months, that is 39 sprints;
• up to 3 random cards per sprint, plus the Friday 5pm outage if prod goes down, with their full effects;
• you can pause at any time.

Your score counts on the global leaderboard and on the Normal mode one.

hiring.body:
Each candidate states the salary they want. Adjust your offer before sending it:

• under 75% of their ask, they always refuse;
• at 110% or more, they always accept;
• in between, it's a negotiation: the closer your offer is to their ask, the more likely they accept.

The team is limited by the office size: 2 people in the garage, 6 at Seed, 15 at Series A, 30 as a Unicorn. A salary is paid every month: hire when your cash can keep up.

INTERNS_ONLY.body:
Here, every candidate is an intern. Each one states the salary they ask for. Set your offer before sending it:

• below 75% of the ask, they always refuse;
• at 110% or more, they always accept;
• in between, it is a negotiation.

The team size depends on the office: 2 people in the garage, 6 at Seed, 15 at Series A, 30 as a Unicorn.
